My alarm rings loudly.
It is morning, but it is still dark.
I open my eyes.
I look out toward the window.
It is completely black outside.
The sun is not up at all.
It is midwinter in Denmark.
It is incredibly dark in the morning here.
It becomes light very late.
I slowly sit up in bed.
It is cold in the apartment.
I turn on the lamp on the table.
It immediately becomes nice with a little light.
Outside the window, the sky is still completely black.
In Mexico there is often a lot of sunlight now.
But here the sun is sleeping.
It is hard to wake up in the dark.
I look at the clock.
I get out of bed.
The day begins now.
